{"id":1127,"level":80,"name":"Форсовані шахи","group":"Форсування","format":27,"description":"<p>Ordinary chess players are often in awe about the amazing combinations masters can come up with. How do these top players do this? The key is in knowing what themes to look for. And the good news is: you can do it too! Well, you won&rsquo;t be an instant grandmaster, but with a bit of practice and study you will know what themes to look for as well.</p>  <p>For example, a master may look for ways of forking his opponent&rsquo;s pieces. If this is not immediately possible, he will think of a combination (often several moves long) that results in a fork.</p>  <p>Every chess player can come up with amazingly complex combinations. How? By learning to think in terms of <em>forcing moves</em>. Forcing moves are moves that force your opponent to choose from a (very) limited set of options.</p>  <p>There are five major types of forcing moves:</p>  <ul>  <li><strong>Checks</strong></li>  <li><strong>Captures</strong></li>  <li><strong>Attacking pieces</strong>&nbsp;(threaten to win material)</li>  <li><strong>Mate threats</strong></li>  <li><strong>Pawn promotions</strong></li>  </ul>  <h3>What do you have to do?</h3>  <p>This exercise lets you practice the first type of forcing moves: giving check. Use checks to win material.</p>","assignment":"","stickerID":97,"examples":[{"fen":"2kr1b1r/4npp1/2q1p3/p1B1P3/2p2Pp1/P1P5/1P2N1QP/3R1RK1 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%cal Ge7c6,Rg2c6]} 1. Rxd8+ Kxd8 2. Bxe7+ {[%cal Re7c6]} Bxe7 3. Qxc6 1-0","text":"<p>На даний момент чорний ферзь закрита, але ми можемо змінити це за допомогою комбінації примусових взяттів і шахів. Спочатку білі беруть d8, щоб перетягнути короля на несприятливе поле. Потім білі шахом беруть коня. Раптом чорний ферзь стає незахищеним, і білі виграють матеріал.</p>","format":27},{"fen":"5k2/7p/b3p1p1/q7/3Q3P/1r3PK1/6P1/7R w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Rb3]} 1. Qf6+ Kg8 2. Qxe6+ {[%cal Ge6g8,Ge6b3]} Kg7 3. Qxb3 1-0","text":"<p>Чорна тура незахищена і є мішенню. Серією точних шахів білі форсують послідовність, яка виграє туру.</p>","format":27},{"fen":"4k3/1R4K1/2r3p1/1p4B1/7P/8/8/1r6 w - - 0 1","pgn":"1. Re7+ Kd8 {[%csl Rb1][%cal Gg5d8]} 2. Re1+ Kd7 3. Rxb1 1-0","text":"<p>Цього разу тура на b1 незахищена. Ми можемо виграти цю туру, використовуючи відкритий чек!</p>","format":27}],"puzzles":[{"id":51022,"fen":"5rk1/pq4b1/1p1pP1P1/n4p2/5Np1/4BP2/P1Q2K2/7R b - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Re3,Rf3]} 1... Qxf3+ (1... Re8?   2. Qe2 =) 2. Kg1 Qxe3+ 0-1","format":27,"texts":[],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":50064,"fen":"7k/p1b2p1P/1p2p1p1/2p1N3/8/2P1B2b/PPP4P/6K1 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Rh3,Rh8]} 1. Nxf7+ Kxh7 (1... Kg7?   2. h8=Q+) 2. Ng5+ Kg7 3. Nxh3 1-0","format":27,"texts":[],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":41274,"fen":"8/8/5rp1/p6k/K4P1p/6PP/8/6R1 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Gg3]} {Q=1} 1. g4+ Kh6 {Q=2} 2. g5+ Kg7 {Q=3} 3. gxf6+ 1-0","format":27,"texts":["Існує загроза форка!","Час провести вилку!","Час заробляти!"],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":51155,"fen":"8/3k1p2/4p3/8/6PQ/5q1P/3r1P1K/1R6 b - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Rh2]} 1... Rxf2+ 2. Kg1 (2. Qxf2 Qxf2+) 2... Qg2# (2... Rg2+?  ) (2... Rd2?  ) (2... Rc2?  ) 0-1","format":27,"texts":[],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":49877,"fen":"2n3k1/5p2/8/4q1pP/2prP1P1/2Q2P2/5K2/4BR2 b - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Rc3,Rf2]} 1... Qh2+ 2. Ke3 Rd3+ 0-1","format":27,"texts":[],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":39419,"fen":"6k1/2b4p/1n2pBp1/8/1q2P3/p2P1R1P/B5P1/7K w - - 0 1","pgn":"1. Bxe6+ Kf8 2. Bc3+ Ke7 3. Bxb4+ 1-0","format":27,"texts":[],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":50112,"fen":"4r3/7R/2kb3p/p2p2p1/P2n1p2/2B2PP1/2P2K1P/5N2 b - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Rf2]} 1... Re2+ 2. Kg1 Nxf3+ {[%csl Rc2,Rf1,Rg1,Rh2]} (2... Kc5?  ) ( 2... Bc5?  ) 0-1","format":27,"texts":[],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":50880,"fen":"7R/8/8/6k1/4p3/5pKP/5P2/4r3 b - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Rf2,Rg3]} 1... Rg1+ 2. Kh